      "problem": "Find the value of $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ cubed.",
      "worked_solution": "To work out $\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^3,$ we multiply $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ by itself and then multiply the result by $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ again:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{3} & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3\\cdot 3}{5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{125}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
